Build type: configure (autotools, ships a generated ./configure)
Source: https://sourceware.org/elfutils/ftp/0.178/elfutils-0.178.tar.bz2
        file_size=9007557 file_md5=5480d0b7174446aba13a6adde107287f
Build order: foundation, before Mesa 25.3.6 (mesa-core/Mesa). Nothing else in
this repo builds against it.
Ported from the canonical GoboLinux recipe ELFUtils/0.178 (Lucas C. Villa Real,
24 Feb 2020); the URL, file_size and file_md5 are identical to upstream and to
the tarball actually used for the ISO's /Programs/ELFUtils/0.178.
Version pinned to 0.178 on purpose. CheckDependencies treats a bare dependency
line as satisfied by ANY installed version, so the only reason this recipe
exists is to make the graph complete: without it, `dependency('libelf')` in
Mesa fails on a host that does not already have the Program. Bumping it would
rebuild a base-system library for no benefit.
configure_options:
 --enable-deterministic-archives  ar/ranlib use -D by default (reproducible).
 --disable-debuginfod             do NOT build the debuginfod *server* (it pulls
                                  libmicrohttpd/libcurl/sqlite/libarchive). The
                                  debuginfod *client* library libdebuginfod is
                                  still built, which is why the installed tree
                                  has lib/pkgconfig/libdebuginfod.pc.
pre_build strips -Werror. elfutils turns every warning into an error from
config/eu.am's AM_CFLAGS
(`... $(if $($(*F)_no_Werror),,-Werror) ...`, with no --disable-werror), and
this 2019 code predates warnings a modern GCC reports -- e.g.
libebl/ebl_syscall_abi.c: `argument 5 of type 'int *' declared as a pointer
[-Werror=array-parameter=]` (libebl.h:248 declares it `int args[6]`).
The sed has to target **Makefile.in**, not Makefile: Compile runs the pre_build
hook BEFORE do_configuration, so a freshly unpacked tree has only Makefile.in,
and that is what config.status copies into Makefile (the -Werror text is plain
make syntax with no @substitutions@, so it survives verbatim).  Touching
Makefile.in also keeps it newer than Makefile.am/eu.am, so automake is not
re-run and the flag is not restored.  Existing Makefile files are patched too,
for the pkgforced --keep case where the tree is already configured.
Reproduced with GCC 16.2.1 (the same error), and the object builds clean with
the flag removed; config.status regeneration of libebl/Makefile after the sed
leaves 0 -Werror.
Optional compression backends are auto-detected by configure (--with-zlib,
--with-bzlib, --with-lzma are all default-on when the headers are present).
The ISO build has zlib, bzip2 and liblzma, so the resulting libdw links
libz/liblzma/libbz2 exactly like /Programs/ELFUtils/0.178/lib/libdw.so does.
Output: lib/libelf.so.1 (+ libelf.pc), lib/libdw.so.1 (+ libdw.pc),
lib/libasm.so.1, lib/libdebuginfod.so, include/{elf.h,gelf.h,libelf.h,dwarf.h},
include/elfutils/*, and the eu-* tools (elfutils' own configure defaults to
--program-prefix=eu-, which is why the binaries are eu-readelf, eu-nm, ...).
